# `prettier --check .` walks the whole tree now that the format scripts are no
# longer limited to src/ and test/, so anything not ours to format has to be
# named here. Everything below is generated: dist/ and public/ are build
# output, coverage/ is a test artefact, and package-lock.json is written by npm
# — its formatting is npm's to choose, not ours.
#
# Nothing else belongs here. Prettier already skips extensions it has no
# parser for (the .png screenshots, assets/logo.svg), so listing those would
# only be config that never does anything.
node_modules/
dist/
public/
coverage/
package-lock.json
